The '''Mar Menor Works''' ({{Langx|ca|Les Obres del Mar Menor}}; {{Langx|scn|L'Òpiri di lu Mar Menor}}) is a man-made system of {{W|dam}}s and [[w:Levee|dikes]], {{W|land reclamation}} and water drainage work, in total the largest {{W|hydraulic engineering}} project undertaken in the [[Baliscan Confederation]] during the twentieth century. The ongoing project involved the damming of the [[Garrigàs Gulf]], a large, shallow [[W:Inlet|inlet]] of the [[Salsipuedes Sea]] between the [[Aprica]]n and [[Canyars|Canyaran]] peninsulas, and the reclamation of land in the newly enclosed water using {{W|polder}}s. Its main purposes are to improve {{W|flood protection}} and create additional land for agriculture and residential development to ease existing land shortages in [[Estuaria]].
